[0.421, "o", "========================================================================\r\nlecture.mp4\r\n========================================================================\r\nLength            00:00:28\r\nPicture every     2 seconds\r\nPictures          14\r\nDescribed         0\r\nTranscript lines  7\r\nSections          1\r\n\r\nEverything below is in the order it happened. Times are from the start\r\nof the video.\r\n\r\n\r\n── Unlabelled stretch (00:00:00 to 00:00:28) ──\r\n00:00:00  Right, so the point of this whole section is that a moving average is not a prediction.\r\n00:00:05  It is a summary of what already happened, smoothed out.\r\n00:00:08  People get into trouble when they treat it as a forecast.\r\n00:00:11  [nobody speaking · 7 seconds]\r\n00:00:18  Now, the crossover everyone talks about, here is what it actually tells you.\r\n00:00:23  It tells you the short average has moved above the long one.\r\n00:00:26  That is all it tells you.\r\n"]
